IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part14-authorisation.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 14, ss 366 to 368: the authorisation a company needs for a
-- political donation or political expenditure, the form of the authorising resolution, and how long it lasts
-- (lines 4693-4736 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN as explained in coa8-part14-meanings.l4 (JUST FALSE only where the text says no).
-- The resolution of the members is asked as a seam from section 281 (coa7): the kind of resolution the text leaves
-- unspecified is "an ordinary resolution unless the company's articles require a higher majority" (s 281(3)).

§ `Authorisation required for donations or expenditure`

-- ---- s 366 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4705 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2)(b)(ii) a “relevant holding company” means a company that, at the time the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred—
-- src:4706 | (a) was a holding company of the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred,
-- src:4707 | (b) was a UK-registered company, and
-- src:4708 | (c) was not a subsidiary of another UK-registered company.
@ref s 366(4) Relevant holding company (src:4705-4708)
-- The facts are judged "at the time the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred" (see s 379(2) for that time).
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred is a subsidiary of the other company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1158 the other company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) the other company is a subsidiary of another UK-registered company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(4) the other company is a relevant holding company` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “relevant holding company” means a company that"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a subsidiary answer (section 1159) is not known
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 1159(1) the company by which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred is a subsidiary of the other company`
        (`s 362 helper both answers` (JUST `s 1158 the other company is a UK-registered company`)
            (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 1159(1) the other company is a subsidiary of another UK-registered company`))

-- src:4704 | (3) No resolution is required on the part of a company that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of a UK-registered company.
@ref s 366(3) No resolution on the part of a wholly-owned subsidiary of a UK-registered company (src:4704)
GIVEN `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1158 the other company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(3) no resolution is required on the part of the company` MEANS
    IF `s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` AND `s 1158 the other company is a UK-registered company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company that is a wholly-owned subsidiary of a UK-registered company"

-- src:4699 | (2) The donation or expenditure must be authorised—
-- src:4700 | (a) in the case of a company that is not a subsidiary of another company, by a resolution of the members of the company;
-- src:4701 | (b) in the case of a company that is a subsidiary of another company by—
-- src:4702 | (i) a resolution of the members of the company, and
-- src:4703 | (ii) a resolution of the members of any relevant holding company.
@ref s 366(2) Who must authorise the donation or expenditure (src:4699-4703)
-- (a) a company that is not a subsidiary: a resolution of its members; (b) a subsidiary: a resolution of its members and
-- a resolution of the members of any relevant holding company. Subsection (3) removes the company's own resolution for a
-- wholly-owned subsidiary of a UK-registered company.
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of another company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 281 a resolution of the members of the company has been passed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 366(3) no resolution is required on the part of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 281 the resolutions of the members of every relevant holding company have been passed` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(2) the donation or expenditure is authorised as section 366(2) requires` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The donation or expenditure must be authorised"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where an answer from another section is not known
    CONSIDER `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of another company`
    WHEN JUST sub THEN
        IF sub
        THEN `s 362 helper both answers` `the company's own resolution is required and passed, or is not required`
                                         (`s 362 helper every answer` `s 281 the resolutions of the members of every relevant holding company have been passed`)
        ELSE `s 281 a resolution of the members of the company has been passed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 362 helper both answers` NOTHING `the company's own resolution is required and passed, or is not required`
    WHERE
        -- subsection (3) gives relief only when it answers JUST TRUE; its NOTHING means "no relief here", so the own resolution is then required
        `the company's own resolution is required and passed, or is not required` MEANS
            IF `s 366(3) no resolution is required on the part of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE `s 281 a resolution of the members of the company has been passed`

-- src:4709 | (5) The resolution or resolutions required by this section—
-- src:4710 | (a) must comply with section 367 (form of authorising resolution), and
-- src:4711 | (b) must be passed before the donation is made or the expenditure incurred.
@ref s 366(5) The resolution or resolutions: form and timing (src:4709-4711)
-- "Passed before the donation is made or the expenditure incurred": a day strictly before the (s 379(2)) time.
GIVEN `the resolution complies with section 367` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the dates on which the resolutions were passed` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the date on which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(5) the resolution or resolutions meet the requirements of subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF null `the dates on which the resolutions were passed`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no resolution has been passed, so there is none for subsection (5) to test
    ELSE `s 362 helper both answers` `the resolution complies with section 367`
            (JUST (all (GIVEN d YIELD d LESS THAN `the date on which the donation was made or the expenditure was incurred`) `the dates on which the resolutions were passed`))
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be passed before the donation is made or the expenditure incurred"

-- src:4712 | (6) Nothing in this section enables a company to be authorised to do anything that it could not lawfully do apart from this section.
@ref s 366(6) Nothing enables a company to be authorised to do what it could not lawfully do (src:4712)
GIVEN `the company could lawfully do it apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(6) section 366 enables the company to be authorised to do it` MEANS
    IF `the company could lawfully do it apart from this section`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only withholds power the company lacks apart from the section
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section enables a company to be authorised to do anything that it could not lawfully do apart from this section"

-- src:4695 | (1) A company must not—
-- src:4696 | (a) make a political donation to a political party or other political organisation, or to an independent election candidate, or
-- src:4697 | (b) incur any political expenditure,
-- src:4698 | unless the donation or expenditure is authorised in accordance with the following provisions.
@ref s 366(1) Authorisation required for donations or expenditure (src:4695-4698)
-- "unless the donation or expenditure is authorised in accordance with the following provisions": JUST TRUE means the company
-- is forbidden. The exemptions of ss 374 to 378 ("authorisation under this Part is not needed") are other sections' answers
-- and are combined by the caller (the seat layer does so).
GIVEN `the company makes a political donation to a political party or other political organisation, or to an independent election candidate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company incurs political expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the donation or expenditure is authorised in accordance with the following provisions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(1) the company is forbidden to make the donation or incur the expenditure` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company makes a political donation to a political party or other political organisation, or to an independent election candidate` OR `the company incurs political expenditure`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only a political donation and political expenditure
    ELSE `s 362 helper the opposite answer` `the donation or expenditure is authorised in accordance with the following provisions`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the donation or expenditure is authorised in accordance with the following provisions"

-- ---- s 367: form of authorising resolution ------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 367(1) what the resolution relates to` IS ONE OF
    `s 367(1)(a) the company passing the resolution`
    `s 367(1)(b) one or more subsidiaries of that company`
    `s 367(1)(c) the company passing the resolution and one or more subsidiaries of that company`
    `s 367(1) some other company`

-- src:4714 | (1) A resolution conferring authorisation for the purposes of this Part may relate to—
-- src:4715 | (a) the company passing the resolution,
-- src:4716 | (b) one or more subsidiaries of that company, or
-- src:4717 | (c) the company passing the resolution and one or more subsidiaries of that company.
@ref s 367(1) A resolution may relate to the company, its subsidiaries, or both (src:4714-4717)
GIVEN relates IS A `s 367(1) what the resolution relates to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367(1) the resolution may relate to` MEANS
    CONSIDER relates
    WHEN `s 367(1)(a) the company passing the resolution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 367(1)(b) one or more subsidiaries of that company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 367(1)(c) the company passing the resolution and one or more subsidiaries of that company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 367(1) some other company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may relate to— (a) the company passing the resolution, (b) one or more subsidiaries of that company, or (c)"

-- src:4718 | (2) A resolution may be expressed to relate to all companies that are subsidiaries of the company passing the resolution—
-- src:4719 | (a) at the time the resolution is passed, or
-- src:4720 | (b) at any time during the period for which the resolution has effect,
-- src:4721 | without identifying them individually.
@ref s 367(2) A resolution may relate to all subsidiaries without identifying them (src:4718-4721)
GIVEN `expressed to relate to all companies that are subsidiaries of the company passing the resolution at the time the resolution is passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `expressed to relate to all companies that are subsidiaries of the company passing the resolution at any time during the period for which the resolution has effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367(2) the resolution may be expressed to relate to all the subsidiaries without identifying them individually` MEANS
    IF `expressed to relate to all companies that are subsidiaries of the company passing the resolution at the time the resolution is passed` OR `expressed to relate to all companies that are subsidiaries of the company passing the resolution at any time during the period for which the resolution has effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the time the resolution is passed, or at any time during the period for which the resolution has effect"

DECLARE `s 367(3) head` IS ONE OF
    `s 367(3)(a) donations to political parties or independent election candidates`
    `s 367(3)(b) donations to political organisations other than political parties`
    `s 367(3)(c) political expenditure`
    `s 367(3) some other head`

-- src:4722 | (3) The resolution may authorise donations or expenditure under one or more of the following heads—
-- src:4723 | (a) donations to political parties or independent election candidates;
-- src:4724 | (b) donations to political organisations other than political parties;
-- src:4725 | (c) political expenditure.
@ref s 367(3) The heads under which a resolution may authorise (src:4722-4725)
GIVEN head IS A `s 367(3) head`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367(3) the resolution may authorise donations or expenditure under the head` MEANS
    CONSIDER head
    WHEN `s 367(3)(a) donations to political parties or independent election candidates` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 367(3)(b) donations to political organisations other than political parties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 367(3)(c) political expenditure` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 367(3) some other head` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under one or more of the following heads"

-- src:4726 | (4) The resolution must specify a head or heads—
-- src:4727 | (a) in the case of a resolution under subsection (2), for all of the companies to which it relates taken together;
-- src:4728 | (b) in the case of any other resolution, for each company to which it relates.
@ref s 367(4) The resolution must specify a head or heads (src:4726-4728)
GIVEN `the resolution is one under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a head or heads are specified for all of the companies to which it relates taken together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a head or heads are specified for each company to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367(4) the resolution specifies the head or heads as required` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is one under subsection (2)`
    THEN IF `a head or heads are specified for all of the companies to which it relates taken together`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution must specify a head or heads— (a) in the case of a resolution under subsection (2), for all of the companies to which it relates taken together"
    ELSE IF `a head or heads are specified for each company to which it relates`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of any other resolution, for each company to which it relates"

-- src:4729 | (5) The resolution must be expressed in general terms conforming with subsection (3) and must not purport to authorise particular donations or expenditure.
@ref s 367(5) General terms, not particular donations or expenditure (src:4729)
GIVEN `expressed in general terms conforming with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `purports to authorise particular donations or expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367(5) the resolution is expressed in general terms as required` MEANS
    IF `expressed in general terms conforming with subsection (3)` AND (NOT `purports to authorise particular donations or expenditure`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be expressed in general terms conforming with subsection (3) and must not purport to authorise particular donations or expenditure"

-- src:4730 | (6) For each of the specified heads the resolution must authorise donations or, as the case may be, expenditure up to a specified amount in the period for which the resolution has effect (see section 368).
@ref s 367(6) A specified amount for each head (src:4730)
GIVEN `for each of the specified heads the resolution authorises donations or expenditure up to a specified amount in the period for which it has effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367(6) the resolution authorises up to a specified amount for each head` MEANS
    IF `for each of the specified heads the resolution authorises donations or expenditure up to a specified amount in the period for which it has effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the resolution must authorise donations or, as the case may be, expenditure up to a specified amount"

-- src:4731 | (7) The resolution must specify such amounts—
-- src:4732 | (a) in the case of a resolution under subsection (2), for all of the companies to which it relates taken together;
-- src:4733 | (b) in the case of any other resolution, for each company to which it relates.
@ref s 367(7) The resolution must specify the amounts (src:4731-4733)
GIVEN `the resolution is one under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `amounts are specified for all of the companies to which it relates taken together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `amounts are specified for each company to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367(7) the resolution specifies the amounts as required` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is one under subsection (2)`
    THEN IF `amounts are specified for all of the companies to which it relates taken together`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution must specify such amounts— (a) in the case of a resolution under subsection (2), for all of the companies to which it relates taken together"
    ELSE IF `amounts are specified for each company to which it relates`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of any other resolution, for each company to which it relates"

-- s 366(5)(a) asks whether the resolution "complies with section 367 (form of authorising resolution)": all of subsections
-- (1) and (3) to (7) must hold (subsection (2) is a permission that widens (1) and adds no condition of its own).
-- src:4713 | 367 Form of authorising resolution
-- src:4714 | (1) A resolution conferring authorisation for the purposes of this Part may relate to—
-- src:4715 | (a) the company passing the resolution,
-- src:4716 | (b) one or more subsidiaries of that company, or
-- src:4717 | (c) the company passing the resolution and one or more subsidiaries of that company.
-- src:4718 | (2) A resolution may be expressed to relate to all companies that are subsidiaries of the company passing the resolution—
-- src:4719 | (a) at the time the resolution is passed, or
-- src:4720 | (b) at any time during the period for which the resolution has effect,
-- src:4721 | without identifying them individually.
-- src:4722 | (3) The resolution may authorise donations or expenditure under one or more of the following heads—
-- src:4723 | (a) donations to political parties or independent election candidates;
-- src:4724 | (b) donations to political organisations other than political parties;
-- src:4725 | (c) political expenditure.
-- src:4726 | (4) The resolution must specify a head or heads—
-- src:4727 | (a) in the case of a resolution under subsection (2), for all of the companies to which it relates taken together;
-- src:4728 | (b) in the case of any other resolution, for each company to which it relates.
-- src:4729 | (5) The resolution must be expressed in general terms conforming with subsection (3) and must not purport to authorise particular donations or expenditure.
-- src:4730 | (6) For each of the specified heads the resolution must authorise donations or, as the case may be, expenditure up to a specified amount in the period for which the resolution has effect (see section 368).
-- src:4731 | (7) The resolution must specify such amounts—
-- src:4732 | (a) in the case of a resolution under subsection (2), for all of the companies to which it relates taken together;
-- src:4733 | (b) in the case of any other resolution, for each company to which it relates.
@ref s 367 Form of authorising resolution (src:4713-4733)
GIVEN `the answer under subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367 the resolution is in the form section 367 requires` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution must" (subsections (4) to (7)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) where subsection (1) is NOTHING
    `s 362 helper every answer` (LIST `the answer under subsection (1)`, `the answer under subsection (4)`, `the answer under subsection (5)`, `the answer under subsection (6)`, `the answer under subsection (7)`)

-- ---- s 368: period for which resolution has effect -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4736 | (2) The power of the directors to make a determination under this section is subject to any provision of the articles that operates to prevent them from doing so.
@ref s 368(2) The directors' power to determine a shorter period (src:4736)
GIVEN `a provision of the articles operates to prevent the directors from determining a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(2) the directors have power to determine a shorter period` MEANS
    IF `a provision of the articles operates to prevent the directors from determining a shorter period`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to any provision of the articles that operates to prevent them from doing so"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The date on which a period of the stated length, beginning on a day, ends: the day before its anniversary in the unit.
-- Working days cannot be counted without the bank holidays of the place (section 1173(1), keel), so they answer NOTHING.
GIVEN beginning IS A DATE
      length IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 368 the last day of a period of the length beginning on` MEANS
    CONSIDER length's unit
    WHEN Days THEN JUST (beginning PLUS length's `number of units` MINUS 1)
    WHEN Weeks THEN JUST (beginning PLUS length's `number of units` TIMES 7 MINUS 1)
    WHEN Months THEN JUST (`add months` beginning (length's `number of units`) MINUS 1)
    WHEN Years THEN JUST (`add years` beginning (length's `number of units`) MINUS 1)
    WHEN `Working days` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the days that count as working days are s 1173(1)'s, which need a place and a calendar

-- src:4735 | (1) A resolution conferring authorisation for the purposes of this Part has effect for a period of four years beginning with the date on which it is passed unless the directors determine, or the articles require, that it is to have effect for a shorter period beginning with that date.
@ref s 368(1) Period for which resolution has effect (src:4735)
-- "four years beginning with the date on which it is passed unless the directors determine, or the articles require, that
-- it is to have effect for a shorter period beginning with that date". The earlier end governs when both are given.
GIVEN passed IS A DATE
      `a shorter period determined by the directors` IS A MAYBE Period
      `the directors have power to determine a shorter period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a shorter period required by the articles` IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 368(1) the last day on which the resolution has effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a shorter period required by the articles`
    WHEN JUST fromArticles THEN
        CONSIDER `a shorter period determined by the directors`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 368 the last day of a period of the length beginning on` passed fromArticles
        WHEN JUST fromDirectors THEN
            CONSIDER `the directors have power to determine a shorter period`
            WHEN JUST power THEN
                IF power
                THEN `s 368 the earlier of two last days` (`s 368 the last day of a period of the length beginning on` passed fromArticles) (`s 368 the last day of a period of the length beginning on` passed fromDirectors)
                ELSE `s 368 the last day of a period of the length beginning on` passed fromArticles
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the articles prevent the directors' determination is not known
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `a shorter period determined by the directors`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`add years` passed 4 MINUS 1) -- the default: "a period of four years beginning with the date on which it is passed"
        WHEN JUST fromDirectors THEN
            CONSIDER `the directors have power to determine a shorter period`
            WHEN JUST power THEN
                IF power
                THEN `s 368 the last day of a period of the length beginning on` passed fromDirectors
                ELSE JUST (`add years` passed 4 MINUS 1) -- the directors' determination is subject to the articles (subsection (2)); without the power the four years stand
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the articles prevent the directors' determination is not known

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 368 the earlier of two last days` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST y THEN
            IF x LESS THAN y
            THEN JUST x
            ELSE JUST y

-- src:4735 | (1) A resolution conferring authorisation for the purposes of this Part has effect for a period of four years beginning with the date on which it is passed unless the directors determine, or the articles require, that it is to have effect for a shorter period beginning with that date.
@ref s 368(1) Period for which resolution has effect (src:4735)
GIVEN `the last day on which the resolution has effect` IS A MAYBE DATE
      passed IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(1) the resolution has effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day on which the resolution has effect`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period of effect is not known
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        IF day AT LEAST passed AND day AT MOST lastDay
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has effect for a period of four years beginning with the date on which it is passed"
